==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Vendor Cat and Kitten''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Tourist Cat''' when obtained from [[Revenge of the Dreamer (Merciless)|Revenge of the Dreamer]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Use this unit to stall and push back strong Traitless enemies with slow attack rates or strong pushers like [[THE SLOTH]], [[R.Ost]] or even [[Camelle]]. This helps your Cats land additional hits in instances where they would usually die from the enemy's attack. If the Traitless enemy is not heavily supported, you can use Lone Cat and Kitten to push it all the way back to the [[Enemy Bases|enemy base]], and if it works, destroy the base without killing the enemy. Lone Cat's freeze can also have utility against [[Henry]], as if they attack at the right moment, they can reset Henry's attack and buy time for units to escape Henry's freeze.

Lone Cat is also extremely useful for cheesing [[Cat God]] and [[Final Boss Giga-God]], since the unit is Immune to Knockback and Warp, with a fast foreswing that allows it to easily interrupt their attack animations.

Beware that like most [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|Cats with knockback]], Lone Cat does have the potential to move forward into the range of other enemies, or make other Cats miss their attacks, though their Single Attack means it is a bit less of an issue.

==='''True Form'''===
Tourist Cat gains higher health and a longer freeze duration. This, by itself, doesn't bring much improvement but buys more time to chain or follow up with additional status effects or damage. This also makes it much easier for him to survive some attacks or to stall Traitless enemies for very long when paired with certain other Cats, notably [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] or [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Crystal Cat]], as they can each cover the same niche, greatly reducing status effect downtime against dangerous Traitless foes. One prominent example is [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]], where Tourist can hit [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|Hermit Cat]], buying time for Healer to follow up, eventually pinning him against the base.

